WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Every journey has a beginning.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.920
Mine started in a small village in India, with a big ambition

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.300
to build a future through learning.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.900
I completed my Electrical and Electronics Engineering degree.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.950
It taught me to think in systems,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.750
trace a problem to its source, and look for evidence,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.750
not assumptions.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.820
My first turn into software was software testing.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.780
What began as a way to understand whether technology worked

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.920
became a craft:

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.550
finding what could fail before it mattered to someone.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.550
Over eighteen years, that craft grew into

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.100
automation architecture, release leadership,

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.050
global team mentoring and AI quality engineering,

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.150
helping teams ship with stronger evidence and confidence.

